<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry IV, Holy Roman Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1050–<a href="/years/1106">1106</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry IV, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a>, was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> from 1056 and emperor from 1084. His clash with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-vii">Pope Gregory VII</a> over the appointment of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> began the Investiture Controversy, and he did penance at Canossa in 1077. He also fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> rebellion, an episode described by the chronicler Lampert of Hersfeld, and was eventually deposed by his son.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-iv-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="Henry IV, Holy Roman Emperor" width="247" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heinrich_4_g.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
